Z||000014||gusto||12-28-2001||01:04 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fiero*101:<BR><B>Ok my last i was being a Jack a$$.<BR>Sorry. I just looked at the specs on the Supra at <A HREF="http://www.Supras.com" TARGET=_blank>www.Supras.com</A> <P>Bone stock the Supra Mk4 makes 225 horse power<BR>the Twin Turbo makes 320<BR>So what kind of Supra is it? <P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>He has a MarkIII. Late 80's, I think its a 86 or 87. Turbo charged w/twin cams. manuel trans. Completely stock. Mine is a 85 SE 6cyl w/auto trans. I'm a much better driver than him though <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. Two weeks ago I watch him stall out in a parking lot. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> The funniest thing in the world is to see a kid who thinks he can drive a stick, stall and try to get going again. BTW how much would a N* conversion cost?||||reg||1
Z||000015||Master_Sushi||12-28-2001||01:54 PM||||Mmmmmmmmm! I love the MKIII supras. I *will* have one some day. Right now fieros fit my budget a bit better though. The mk3 turbo supras are very fast cars. I have heard from the supras forums that the autos have better times then the 5 speeds. I'd just love to run one of them through the gears. DOHC, inline six, turbo, 7000rpm redline, 232hp stock, I think they had 250 ft lbs of torque (but im not 100% sure on that). Smooth!<P>They are somewhat expensive cars to keep runing well. But they have a huge aftermarket for them. They can be made into 12 second cars pretty easily. They are like 15 sec stock. <P>The non turbos would probably be a close race with a stock V6 fiero. But its its a turbo I dought a stock fiero has much of a chance keeping up. Maybe off the line for a few secs... But a fiero cant do 160mph. lol||||reg||4
Z||000016||FieroKyle||12-28-2001||02:42 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by gusto:<BR><B> Two weeks ago I watch him stall out in a parking lot.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> The funniest thing in the world is to see a kid who thinks he can drive a stick, stall and try to get going again</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Hey, atleast he is trying to learn a stick other than the other 80% of wussies are there. I am not bashing you at all. When I stall my car it is usually in a parking lot, but hey, you have just get in the car, your not thinking then wham, ya stall it. Rarely stall on the street, never racing, never when trying to burn out. I drive one pretty good, I learned driving on a stick with a Jeep Wrangler and a 94 Chevy Pickup, then a 72' MG Midget. Also have drove a dump truck a few times. But anyways, it is funny for me too watching kids stall it because 80% time they don't know anything about cars or how to drive them.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000017||BlackStang95||12-28-2001||07:38 PM||||Turbo Supras are nice cars, but stock they are not the gods the riceboys think they are.<BR>The fastest year was the 93 and it got<BR>1993   Toyota Supra Turbo                     4.9            13.4<P>Not bad at all, I guess it depends on what you consider "run with".  But it's certainly not enough to beat any stock stang, camaro, vette or viper out there (more than enough to beat a stock fiero though).<P>With mods it is a beast...I've seen ones with over 1000 hp.  <P>However, that costs a lot.  Like they said in the movie, about 20 thousand.  And that was doing all the work themselves.  Performance isnt cheap.<P>And it didn't kill the ferrari...it realisticly barely edged it out.  One could surmise the ferarri driver gave up when they started weaving through oncoming traffic.     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P><p>[This message has been edited by BlackStang95 (edited 12-28-2001).]||||reg||1
